                <pb facs="0492" n="478" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg478"/>

                <head><seg type="margin">[79]</seg><hi rendition="#italic">*Mr. Adams, Secretary of State, to district attorneys</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Circular.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of
                        State</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian" when="1817-12-13"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">December</hi> 13, 1817</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to request you to transmit to this
                    Department, at as early a day as you may find convenient, a statement of every
                    case in which you have, since the last session of Congress, instituted a process
                    before the courts of the United States, for the execution of the laws to enforce
                    a due observance of the neutral obligations of the United States in the contest
                    between Spain and the American Provinces, claimed by her as colonies; specifying
                    those in which you have proceeded in consequence of applications from the
                    Spanish consuls, together with the decisions of the courts in the cases upon
                    which any decision has been had.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN QUINCY ADAMS.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">United States District Attorneys</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">At New Orleans, Georgia, Charleston, South Carolina,
                            Baltimore, Philadelphia, New York, Boston, Portsmouth, and Rhode
                            Island.</hi>
                    </p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
